    "body": "For the maintainer, a judgement call: this PR changes the expectation of one existing heavy-lane test, `verify::envelope_verdict_follows_the_stated_tol`. Its tight half (cone rings laddered for tol 0.1, judged at 0.01) now expects one non-blocking Scallop note (~0.085 mm) instead of silence. The note is real: a 45-degree cone laddered for tol 0.1 leaves ~0.1 mm cusps, and the old reach (4·tol past the ball) was too short to see them. The test's own law still holds: a tighter yardstick invents no envelope defect.\n\nAlternatives considered: (a) keep the old reach, which leaves stepovers between ~2.9 and 6 mm on an r3 ball unread, the #212 gap; (b) hold the scallop note silent under the stated tol only when the generator's ladder tol is looser, which would hide a real cusp the user asked to be judged against. I chose to report it. The note never blocks the post. Marking ready: the gate is green, and no G-code or GUI change needs a user check.",
